{"highest":2,"ids":{"performance lens, medium: All comment pages for the issue are fetched without a server-side time filter; for issues with long comment histories the number of API round-trips and the volume of data written to disk grow linearly with the total comment count. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh: \"if ! rsc_gh \"$sd\" \"$out\" api --paginate --repo \"$slug\" \\\"; happens when: Every gh-backend claim attempt calls `_ccgl_race_note_first_v`; the `--paginate` flag causes rsc_gh to fetch every page of issue comments, then jq discards everything older than `since` client-side. An issue with 150 comments forces 5+ round-trips; `since` is computed but never passed to the API.; fix: code; ACCEPTED IF: only comments potentially within the race-detection window are fetched from GitHub — comments older than the window are excluded at the server before pagination begins.)":"RLPERFORMANCE-1","performance lens, low: When my_holder is provided — which is always the case in the call from claim_coordinator_claim — _ccgl_race_note_first_v runs jq twice on the same temp file: once to find the winner, once to find this run's note id; a single jq invocation could return both values. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh: \"_CCGL_RACE_NOTE_MY_ID=\"$(jq -rs --arg p \"${_CCGL_RACE_NOTE_PREFIX}\" \\\"; happens when: Every gh-backend claim that enters race detection calls _ccgl_race_note_first_v with my_holder set; the second jq process starts and iterates the same filtered comment list on every such call.; fix: code; ACCEPTED IF: a single gh-backend claim attempt that enters race detection calls jq no more than once against the fetched comment data to obtain both the race winner and this run's own note id)":"RLPERFORMANCE-2"}}
